[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704219323","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103675#issuecomment-2704219323","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103675","id":2704219323,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hLxy7","user":{"login":"StaydMcMuffin","id":38304659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzA0NjU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38304659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin","html_url":"https://github.com/StaydMcMuffin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T15:42:53Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T15:42:53Z","body":"This is not a bug or a regression, but the result of a fix contained in #100441. As mentioned in the PR, Godot uses [MikkTSpace](http://www.mikktspace.com/) for calculating the TBN basis vectors for meshes, and the correct way to utilize these vectors is to leave them _unnormalized_ in the fragment shader. If you need the normalized normal vector for _something other than the tangent basis transformation_, it is correct to simply normalize it yourself before use (as a separate variable, of course, so that **NORMAL** itself doesn't get normalized).\nObviously this change is unexpected if you weren't already aware of this specific PR, so, yeah this is a documentation issue. Now that 4.4 stable is out, the docs should be updated to state clearly that these vectors are provided _unnormalized_ so that users can correctly apply the tangent basis transformation themselves if needed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704219323/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704412884","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103675#issuecomment-2704412884","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103675","id":2704412884,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hMhDU","user":{"login":"nickybakes","id":47609027,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NjA5MDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47609027?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickybakes","html_url":"https://github.com/nickybakes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickybakes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickybakes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickybakes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickybakes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickybakes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickybakes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickybakes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickybakes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickybakes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T16:56:56Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T16:56:56Z","body":"> This is not a bug or a regression, but the result of a fix contained in [#100441](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100441)\n\n\nI see. As mentioned in my post, a user on Reddit thought this was the case, but we thought it would be considered a bug because \"In theory the user-facing NORMAL should not have changed though, so this seems like a bug that slipped through\" (from u/godot_clayjohn) ([My Reddit post on this issue](https://www.reddit.com/r/godot/comments/1j36ows/godot_44_normal_builtin_value_in_shaders_is_no/))\n\nIf this value being un-normalized when the user gets to use it is just how its going to be, then I agree with you that its not necessarily a bug and more just a documentation issue.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704412884/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704522774","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103675#issuecomment-2704522774","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103675","id":2704522774,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hM74W","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T17:37:49Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T17:37:49Z","body":"Ya, this is a regression. We shouldn't be breaking user workflows in a minor release. Users should be able to expect that the `NORMAL` built in continues to be normalized. Especially since they may not even be using normal maps. For many users we have broken their project for no tangible gain. \n\nWe just need to figure out what the best solution will be, as we can't make everyone happy at this point. \n\nUser uses `NORMAL`, but not `NORMAL_MAP`: We should use the normalized normal. We are screwed here anyway because the user may write to `NORMAL` and then our MikkTSpace assumptions are out the window\n\nUser does not use `NORMAL` or `NORMAL_MAP`: We can do what we do now","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704522774/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704738413","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103675#issuecomment-2704738413","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103675","id":2704738413,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hNwht","user":{"login":"Lippanon","id":115422160,"node_id":"U_kgDOBuEz0A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115422160?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon","html_url":"https://github.com/Lippanon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lippanon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T19:19:36Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T19:19:36Z","body":"I updated to 4.4 from 4.3 and noticed some shaders look different (they looked like artifacts) and it seems this is the cause.\nI'm commenting to affirm that if the user is now expected to change their shaders it should probably be made clear in a news post besides docs, as part of migration.\nDoes it only affect `NORMAL`, or also `BINORMAL`, and `TANGENT`? I have many shaders and I'd like to search through to fix the visual differences in the meantime, regardless if this will be fixed as a regression or not. Thanks.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704738413/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704997078","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103675#issuecomment-2704997078","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103675","id":2704997078,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hOvrW","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-06T21:36:24Z","updated_at":"2025-03-06T21:36:24Z","body":"> Does it only affect NORMAL, or also BINORMAL, and TANGENT? I have many shaders and I'd like to search through to fix the visual differences in the meantime, regardless if this will be fixed as a regression or not. Thanks.\n\nIt affects all three. Previously they were normalized in the fragment shader after interpolation. Now they are normalized in the Vertex shader before interpolation. If you are using the values for normal mapping, this is typically the behaviour that you want as it will match the assumptions made when baking the normal maps. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2704997078/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2705689479","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103675#issuecomment-2705689479","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103675","id":2705689479,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hRYuH","user":{"login":"pineapplemachine","id":7266412,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNjY0MTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7266412?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine","html_url":"https://github.com/pineapplemachine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pineapplemachine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T07:06:07Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T07:06:07Z","body":"It seems natural for users to expect `NORMAL` to be a unit vector, and I suspect just putting a note otherwise in the documentation won't do very much for the confusion. Especially not given that this is what it used to be, now, before changing.\n\nBut it does seem like a good idea to keep the non-normalized vector accessible in shaders. Would it make sense to introduce a new set of uniforms like `INTERPOLATED_NORMAL`, etc. for the non-normalized versions? Or to perhaps make it a configuration option in the shader Resource for whether to not normalize before passing to fragment shaders?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2705689479/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3072953612","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103675#issuecomment-3072953612","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103675","id":3072953612,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc63KY0M","user":{"login":"QbieShay","id":7917475,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5MTc0NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7917475?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay","html_url":"https://github.com/QbieShay","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/QbieShay/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-15T09:51:45Z","updated_at":"2025-07-15T09:51:45Z","body":"Circling back to this in 4.5 release process. While i agree with @clayjohn that we shouldn't break users workflows - I also feel like this breakage is the less bad option.\n\nNormalizing normals by default, (or doing some magic) will impede some tech art work (it's one more varying available after all). Doing some magic to normalize or not normalize normals will also cause problems, because as those assumption get more and more complicated, they are more bug prone.\n\nAdditionally, most devs that come from other engines already have the reflex to normalize normals, since they aren't normalized in Unity, for example.\n\nIf we want to go the route of non-normalizing them, it should probably be a render mode that when added leaves normals unnormalized.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3072953612/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3082326912","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103675#issuecomment-3082326912","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103675","id":3082326912,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc63uJOA","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-17T03:30:34Z","updated_at":"2025-07-17T03:30:34Z","body":"> If we want to go the route of non-normalizing them, it should probably be a render mode that when added leaves normals unnormalized.\n\nAnother option could be to add a new read-only built-in called `RAW_NORMAL` that would allow users to read from the raw normal value if they want it. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3082326912/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]